I decided that if I'm going to go old school, I'm going to go all the way old school and try to bring back the blogroll.  For now, it's "powered" by a janky hand-export of some of my feed reader's categories, which I need to redo since people are all over the place and the categories kind of no longer make sense - but it works for now (because there's a script that checks to make sure every site is still up)!

{% for category in blogroll.categories %}
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-slate-50 mt-8 mb-2">{{ category.name }}</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 list-none pl-0 ml-0">
  {% for item in category.items %}
  <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
    <img src="https://icons.duckduckgo.com/ip3/{{ item.url | domain }}.ico" alt="" class="w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 relative top-0.5" />
    <span>
      <a href="{{ item.url }}" class="text-primary hover:text-primary-dark dark:text-primary-light dark:hover:text-primary font-medium">{{ item.title }}</a>{% if item.description %}<span class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"> - {{ item.description }}</span>{% endif %}
    </span>
  </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endfor %}
